([Abstract]) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 702 Tm
(BERT: Pre-training of Deep Bidirectional Transformers for Language Understanding) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 669 Tm
(Authors: Jacob Devlin, Ming-Wei Chang, Kenton Lee, Kristina Toutanova \(2019\)) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 636 Tm
(Abstract: We introduce a new language representation model called BERT, which stands) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 621 Tm
(for Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers. Unlike recent language) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 606 Tm
(representation models, BERT is designed to pre-train deep bidirectional) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 591 Tm
(representations from unlabeled text by jointly conditioning on both left and right) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 576 Tm
(context in all layers.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 543 Tm
(As a result, the pre-trained BERT model can be fine-tuned with just one additional) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 528 Tm
(output layer to create state-of-the-art models for a wide range of tasks, such as) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 513 Tm
(question answering and language inference, without substantial task-specific) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 498 Tm
(architecture modifications.) Tj
ET
